{number: 62}
{title: Saved by Grace}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Some day the silver cord will break,
And I no more as [G7] now shall sing;
But [C] oh, the joy when I shall wake
Within the [G7] palace of the [C] King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I shall [F] see Him face to [C] face,
And tell the [G7] story—Saved by [C] grace;
And I shall [F] see Him face to [C] face,
And tell the [G7] story—Saved by [C] grace.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Some day my earthly house will fall,
I cannot tell how [G7] soon ’twill be;
But [C] this I know-—my All in All
Has now a [G7] place in heav’n for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Some day, when fades the golden sun
Beneath the rosy-[G7] tinted west,
My [C] blessed Lord will say, “Well done!”
And I shall [G7] enter into [C] rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Some day: till then I’ll watch and wait,
My lamp all trimmed and [G7] burning bright,
That [C] when my Saviour opens the gate,
My soul to [G7] Him may take its [C] flight.
{end_of_verse}
